gdiplus: Filling closes every figure, also an open one followed by another.

The span code behind software fills added a figure's closing edge only when the figure was explicitly closed or was
the last one of the path. An open figure followed by another left an odd number of edges on its scanlines, and Wine
stopped on the assertion "edge[0].y == edge[1].y" in edge_list_to_spans_alternate: Lightroom Classic's Photo > Edit
In > Open as Layers / Open as Smart Object in Photoshop ended in "Assertion failed" (Wine C++ Runtime Library). On
Windows the fill closes every figure. Repro: wine/tests/gdiplus/openfig.c.

--- a/dlls/gdiplus/region.c
+++ b/dlls/gdiplus/region.c
@@ -1194,7 +1194,9 @@
         {
             stat = line_to_edge_list(path->pathdata.Points[i-1], path->pathdata.Points[i], bounds, edges);
 
-            if (stat == Ok && ((type & PathPointTypeCloseSubpath) || i == path->pathdata.Count - 1))
+            /* filling closes every figure: an open one ends where the next figure starts */
+            if (stat == Ok && ((type & PathPointTypeCloseSubpath) || i == path->pathdata.Count - 1 ||
+                               (path->pathdata.Types[i + 1] & PathPointTypePathTypeMask) == PathPointTypeStart))
                 stat = line_to_edge_list(path->pathdata.Points[i], path->pathdata.Points[subpath_start], bounds, edges);
         }
     }
